cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "viscoelastic-startup: Verification and reproducibility of exact solutions for start-up flows of viscoelastic fluids"
abstract: >-
  Annotated Jupyter notebooks that reproduce, from scratch, published corrections to
  erroneous "exact solutions" for start-up flows of viscoelastic fluids. Each notebook
  states the initial-boundary-value problem, implements the erroneous published solution
  exactly as printed, derives the correct solution, checks both independently against a
  numerical Laplace inversion and a finite-difference solution, and regenerates the
  comparison figure of the paper being corrected. The recurring error is the mishandling
  of the impulsive start-up condition, which turns Stokes' first problem, or the start-up
  of plane Couette flow, into the start-up of a plate ramped on the retardation timescale.
type: software
